{
  "lesson_id": "c1_prepositions_position_and_advanced_patterns",
  "level": "C1",
  "title": "Prepositions: Position and advanced patterns",
  "description": "Prepositions at C1 работают как часть larger patterns. Их нельзя надёжно выводить прямым переводом.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-C1-9-RU",
    "lesson_num": 9,
    "title": "Правила: Prepositions: Position and advanced patterns",
    "level": "C1",
    "overview": "Prepositions at C1 работают как часть larger patterns. Их нельзя надёжно выводить прямым переводом.",
    "main_rule": "Prepositions can follow verbs, adjectives and nouns. In questions/relative clauses they can stay at the end or move before whom/which in formal style. Preposition to is followed by -ing.",
    "form": "verb + prep. adjective + prep. noun + prep. preposition + V-ing. Wh + clause + prep.",
    "when_why": "depend on, belong to, insist on, object to; responsible for, aware of, capable of, interested in; reason for, solution to, effect on, access to.",
    "examples": "I depend on the result. → Я завишу от результата.\nShe is responsible for the project. → Она отвечает за проект.\nWe need a solution to the problem. → Нам нужно решение проблемы.\nWho did you speak to? → С кем ты говорил?\nTo whom did you speak? → С кем вы разговаривали? (formal)\nI'm interested in learning. → Я заинтересован в изучении.\nI look forward to hearing from you. → Жду вашего ответа.",
    "special_cases": "To can be a preposition, not infinitive marker: look forward to hearing, object to paying.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ I look forward to hear from you. → ✅ I look forward to hearing from you.\n❌ access of the system → ✅ access to the system.",
    "dont_confuse": "Учи noun/verb/adjective together with its preposition.",
    "quick_summary": "Verb + prep.\nAdjective + prep.\nNoun + prep.\nPreposition to + V-ing.\nFormal preposition placement → whom/which."
  },
